A||N||9||AusFiero||Anyone got a spare 85 MPH sidelit gauge panel?||||1||
Z||000000||AusFiero||07-27-2001||09:49 PM||||Ok I have had a few requests to produce these as well. The backlit ones are looking very feasible in the OEM quality. Printing tests are underway with the manufacturer. <P>Now what I need is an old 85 MPH gauge panel. Doesn't even need to be a working one, just have intact gauges so I have something to work with to produce a quality set of aftermarket faces.  I cannot afford to pay for it, I am on $0 income since surgery and have been investing money in various projects I really shouldn't be at the moment. Backlit 120 MPH production tests for instance. <P>So heres the deal, if anyone is willing to ship an old gauge set (gut it for weight, I only need the gauges) to Australia I will in turn give them a free set of 85 MPH gauge faces when I produce them in a colour and custom style of their choice.<P>Anyone? Email me if we can do a deal.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000001||pherder||07-27-2001||10:17 PM||||You got mail!<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||07-27-2001||10:41 PM||||How do I tell the difference, Jim? I have several sets lying around and will send you whatever you need...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||AusFiero||07-27-2001||10:56 PM||||I have no idea Songman. I have never ever seen a real set of the 85 MPH ones. Kinda hard with no Fieros around. I already have an offer of an 84 set which I am told are different. So I have accepted them. Maybe have a set of the other 85 plus, will keep you in mind. Thanks.<P>Anyone know if there is a few different ones? I want to cover the whole range of Fieros.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DecadenceR||07-27-2001||11:49 PM||||The 84's are totally different from the 85+... The 84 is a solid metal piece, no backing. it's riveted on. The 85+ is (are?) backlit, and they are differnt appearance wise, and the faces come off like the 120's.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hartz||07-28-2001||12:04 AM||||Actually, I think there are THREE different types of 85 MPH guages.  There are the types that came in '84's.  There's the type that came in '85 SEs and GTs, which are also reflective, but have different graphics on the front.  Then lastly, there are the backlit 85 MPH guages from 86+.<P>I can get some pictues if necessary.<P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo||||reg||1
Z||000006||Hartz||07-28-2001||12:25 AM||||OK, forgive the picture quality - I'm no Ansel Adams here.  But here's the three types of '85 MPH guages I have seen:<P>First, the '84 style:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/84_guage.JPG"> <P>Next, the '85 SE/GT style:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/85_gt_guage.jpg"> <P>Lastly, the nice backlit guages from '86+:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/backlit_guage.jpg"> <P><BR>Note in the pictures that the idiot light overlays are switched on the '84 and '85 pictures.  <P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Steve Normington||07-28-2001||12:40 AM||||You have mail.||||reg||1
Z||000008||b lo 0||07-28-2001||12:43 AM||||I have some sidelit '85 GT gauges if you want 'em.  Speedo's fried.  I need a new gauge panel-I'm looking for a 120 mph backlit panel to replace it, but same prob-zero denero.  If someone wants to donate a 120 set (I can work on electronics, so minor defects are not a problem) I will send Aus my 85 mph set as soon as I get it.  Can't send until I can get new gauges tho.  A little hard to drive (and explain to cops) with no gauge cluster.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1">'85 GT (in progress)<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">      <BR>White Lightnin!  (NOT moonshine, for all you hillbillies!)</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000009||AusFiero||07-28-2001||06:40 AM||||Ok I hae what I need now people...thanks. I will contact the people by email to sort out the final details. I woulda posted this earlier but ended up back in hospital today  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Am alright again now but have to go back again Monday for more scans and stuff.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
